{
  "_comment": "Tag bank in three tiers. Instagram caps a post at five hashtags (December 2025) and Mosseri has said they label a post's topic rather than drive reach, so every post gets four topic tags plus the brand tag. Sales reels carry their own tags in demos.json; this bank serves the other formats through pick_tags and tops up the YouTube description to twelve, in the order below, so keep each tier ordered by evidence. Basis, 17 Sep 2026 audit of about twenty-five competitor and Indian placement reels with verified like counts: the two largest winners (87K and 75K likes) shared exactly #jobinterview #aitools #jobseekers #interview; #interviewtips and #interviewhacks sat on several more. The precise category tags (#aiinterview, #aiinterviewassistant, #interviewcopilot) appeared only on posts under a hundred likes or in YouTube titles, so they keep one slot for what they say about the product, not for reach. Competitor names appeared only as brands tagging themselves; they stay in the YouTube top-up where a slot is cheap. #Cluely is the largest competitor tag but is the 'cheat on everything' brand, the framing _topic_note in pillars.json warns gets accounts actioned, so it stays out. Correlation only: those reels won on their hooks.",
